By exercising a permission granted by this License, you agree to comply with its terms. Components that carry a separate license are governed by that license to the extent stated in Section 8.

1. Definitions

1.1 "Software" means the source code, object code, plugins, modules, documentation, assets, and other materials expressly marked as licensed under the PDL or included in an official Pancake distribution identified as being subject to the PDL. It excludes third-party components and materials governed by separate license terms.

1.2 "Pancake Core" means the software and code developed for the core functionality of Pancake and owned by, or licensed to, the relevant Pancake copyright holder.

1.3 "Pancake Development Team" or "Team" means the project group responsible for developing, maintaining, and operating Pancake.

1.4 "Authorized Team Member" means a person formally recognized by the Team to perform specified project or administrative duties. Team membership alone does not transfer copyright ownership or authorize that person to license rights belonging to another rights holder.

1.5 "Copyright Holder" means the person or entity that owns the applicable copyright or other relevant rights in a particular component of the Software.

1.6 "Plugin" means a software extension, module, command collection, or related functionality developed for or distributed through Pancake.

1.7 "Plugin Author" means the creator, owner, or maintainer of a Plugin or its associated materials, to the extent that person or entity holds the applicable rights.

1.8 "Contribution" means code, documentation, assets, or other material submitted to an official Pancake repository, channel, or contribution mechanism for possible inclusion in Pancake.

1.9 "Official Pancake Services" means the hosted Pancake Discord bot, Pancake Embed Editor, Pancake Plugin Portal, and other services officially operated by the Team under the Pancake name.

1.10 "Written Authorization" means express permission recorded in a verifiable written form, such as an email or signed agreement, from the Copyright Holder or a representative authorized to grant the relevant rights.

1.11 "Commercial Exploitation" means selling, licensing, reselling, redistributing for payment, offering a hosted or competing service based on the Software, or otherwise charging specifically for access to, copies of, or derivative versions of the Software, except as expressly authorized by this License or in writing by the relevant Copyright Holder.

