These restrictions do not prohibit ordinary use of the Official Pancake Services under their applicable terms, nor do they restrict rights that cannot lawfully be restricted under applicable law.

5. Plugins and Plugin Author Rights

5.1 Ownership. Plugin Authors retain ownership of their Plugins and original materials unless a separate written agreement expressly assigns those rights. Unless otherwise agreed, the permissions granted under this Section are non-exclusive, and a Plugin Author remains free to use or license their own work, subject to third-party rights and any separate agreement.

5.2 Permission for official inclusion. By submitting a Plugin for inclusion in an Official Pancake Service or official Pancake distribution, the Plugin Author grants the Team a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license, for the duration of the applicable rights, to host, reproduce, execute, use, integrate, maintain, modify, adapt, and distribute that Plugin as part of the development, operation, maintenance, promotion, and provision of Official Pancake Services and their official distributions. The Team may permit its hosting providers, contractors, and infrastructure providers to exercise these rights only as reasonably necessary to support those activities.

5.3 Scope of permission. The permission in Section 5.2 allows the Team to operate and monetize Official Pancake Services that include or rely on the Plugin, subject to any separate written terms agreed with the Plugin Author. It does not allow the Team to use the Plugin code in unrelated products, bots, or projects outside the Pancake ecosystem without additional Written Authorization from the relevant Copyright Holder.

5.4 Modifications. The Team may modify a Plugin under Section 5.2 for compatibility, maintenance, security, or functionality within Official Pancake Services. Such modifications do not transfer ownership of the original Plugin to the Team. Ownership of separately authored modifications follows applicable law and any separate written agreement; this License does not automatically assign those rights.

5.5 Plugin obligations. A Plugin Author submitting a Plugin represents that they have the rights and authority needed to submit it and grant the permissions stated in this License. The Plugin Author is responsible for identifying relevant third-party components and complying with their license terms.

5.6 Separate Plugin license. If a Plugin is expressly accompanied by a separate license, that license governs the Plugin to the extent of any conflict with the PDL. The PDL does not remove or override rights or obligations arising under a third-party license.

6. Contributions and Contributor License Grant

6.1 Authority. By submitting a Contribution, the Contributor represents that they have the right to submit it and that, to the best of their knowledge, it does not knowingly infringe third-party rights or violate another binding obligation.

6.2 Review permission. By submitting a Contribution through an official Pancake contribution mechanism, the Contributor grants the Team a non-exclusive, royalty-free permission to access, reproduce, test, and evaluate the Contribution solely to determine whether it should be incorporated into Pancake. If the Contribution is rejected and not used, this review permission ends once evaluation is complete, subject to reasonable technical retention and applicable law.

6.3 License for accepted Contributions. When a Contribution is accepted or incorporated into Pancake, the Contributor grants the Team a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license, for the duration of the applicable rights, to use, reproduce, execute, host, maintain, modify, adapt, integrate, and distribute the Contribution as part of the development, operation, maintenance, and official distribution of Pancake. The Team may sublicense these permissions to hosting providers, contractors, and infrastructure providers to the extent reasonably necessary to perform those activities.

6.4 Ownership and limits. The Contributor retains ownership of their Contribution unless a separate written agreement expressly assigns it. The license in Section 6.3 does not authorize the Team to sell or distribute the Contribution as a standalone product, or to use it in unrelated projects outside the Pancake ecosystem, unless the relevant rights holder gives additional Written Authorization or the Team otherwise holds those rights.

6.5 Non-revocation. To the extent permitted by applicable law, the license granted for an accepted Contribution is intended to be perpetual and may not be revoked solely because the Contributor later leaves the project or no longer wishes to contribute. This does not affect any non-waivable rights under applicable law.

6.6 Different licensing terms. The Team may not relicense a Contribution under materially different terms beyond the permissions granted in this Section without the Contributor's further authorization, unless the Team independently owns the relevant rights or otherwise has a lawful basis to do so.

6.7 Separate agreements. A signed contributor agreement or other Written Authorization may supplement or replace this Section for the Contribution it covers.

