9.1 A Copyright Holder may enforce rights that they own. The Team or an Authorized Team Member may submit a complaint, takedown notice, or other request only for rights owned by the Team or for which they have been appropriately authorized to act.

9.2 Depending on the circumstances and applicable law, enforcement may include contacting a hosting provider or platform, submitting a legally available takedown notice (including a DMCA notice where applicable), requesting removal of infringing material, or pursuing other lawful remedies.

9.3 A Team action does not replace or limit a Plugin Author's independent rights in their own work, and a Plugin Author may enforce their own rights subject to applicable law and any relevant agreement.

9.4 Nothing in this License guarantees a particular enforcement outcome or expands any party's legal rights beyond those they actually hold.

10. Termination

10.1 If you materially breach this License, the permissions granted to you may terminate. Where the breach can reasonably be corrected, the relevant Copyright Holder or authorized representative will, where practicable, provide written notice and a reasonable opportunity to cure it. If the breach is not cured within fifteen (15) days after notice, the permissions may terminate.

10.2 Termination may take effect immediately where a breach cannot reasonably be cured, involves deliberate unauthorized distribution or commercial exploitation, or creates an urgent security, legal, or intellectual-property risk, to the extent permitted by applicable law.

10.3 Upon termination, you must stop the use that is no longer authorized and, upon reasonable request, delete or destroy copies under your control to the extent legally required and technically practicable. Termination does not remove rights granted under a separate license for components governed by that license, nor does it undo rights validly granted to the Team under Sections 5 or 6, subject to applicable law and any separate agreement.

10.4 The rights and remedies available under this Section are subject to applicable law.

